WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.800
Anime conventions are a rare enigma where you

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.840
can see herds of wild otaku migrate from the safety of their own homes to a designated

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.160
spot in order to socialize,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.000
interact, and sometimes even breed with their own kind.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.140
[It] can sometimes be intimidating for outsiders looking at the strange lifestyles

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.840
seen at these gatherings.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.140
But as I've been to many cons this year and with cons season almost over

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.820
what is the real experience, I think,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.040
both new and seasoned con-goers should be aware of?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.600
♪~

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.520
Before deciding to go to a convention, know they can cost a fair bit of money.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.260
So budgeting is a very important skill to have.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.620
One commonly suggested budgeting technique

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.940
is to take your entire life savings add the maximum limit to your credit card and -

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.640
[...]

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.260
Now a combination can be expensive

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.800
but you can get around this by rooming with some friends.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.000
If you don't have any real-life friends to room with then the next best

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.280
thing is to find online friends.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:49.800
so lonely = [

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.420
They're like real-life friends except

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.360
you're more familiar with them as a disembodied avatar on your computer screen

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.820
Just be careful as you shouldn't be surprised

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.980
if that one person who appeared all right the two times you talk to them on discord

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.280
suddenly becomes an annoying twat who has seemingly

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.180
never taught any manners by their parents.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.240
The typical estimate on how many people you should share

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.510
accommodation with goes by taking the width and length of a standard hotel room

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.300
calculating the area then dividing that by the number of average human bodies

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.979
that can lay in it side by side.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:15.700
Once you arrive at the con,

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.000
the first challenge you'll have to handle is picking up your badge.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.599
This is a fairly simple procedure for small conventions, but for any larger ones

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.650
you'll need to be ready.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.620
Most cons allow you to pick it up the day before the convention starts.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.119
As if you show up on the opening day,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.100
you'll be expected to wait in line for approximately

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.240
half the life expectancy of an average human being

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.180
while also being subjugated to walk past least 10 fuckers you measure

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.200
the life worth on how many high-fives they can collect -

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.380
- and once you get past that -

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.280
you can finally start enjoying the convention!

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.380
If this is your first time, it may be a surreal experience

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.149
hearing words like kawaii or sugoi or Jojo's reference

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.880
casually being thrown out in public and some people take this

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.400
as a sign that they've just entered a separate dimension of reality,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.340
detached from any and all social norms.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.600
Surprisingly, this is not actually the case

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.060
so be sure to keep in mind that all actions,

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.120
that can make you seem creepy, or rude,

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.560
or downright criminally harassing, in the real world still do apply here.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.000
Cosplayers are one of the most well-known things about conventions

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.060
and you may get excited seeing some of your favorite characters or even your waifu.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.180
Though, be wary.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.180
Is not a widely known fact that cosplayers have personalities emotions, insecurities,

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:16.559
morals, and lives outside of their costumes.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.540
So they are almost just like human beings.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.300
If you want to take a picture the correct social etiquette are:

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.070
go up to the cosplayer ask politely if you can take a picture

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.620
then awkwardly tried to figure out where you're supposed to put your hands.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.200
If you're thinking about cosplaying yourself,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.240
however, then don't forget at the end of every convention

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:37.080
you will be put in a death tournament against everyone else who cosplayed your character

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.840
as only one is allowed to walk out alive.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:39.340
don't go as deadpool

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.210
Spending the entire day at the convention can be draining so it's recommended

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.840
you bring some kind of bag with all the provisions you need.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.800
If you want to be prepared, a rough list of things you'll need is your

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:54.740
con book, schedule, snacks camera, phone charger, hand sanitizer, spare batteries, poster tubes, camping gear, first-aid kits, zombie survival pack, pepper spray, machetes

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:59.120
extra bullets for good luck and most importantly enough liquids to make it through a nuclear winter.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.540
Despite all this, however, there will always be one resource that is in short supply.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.600
This is body spray.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:11.740
It is a device that can be applied on the body which can temporarily mask out odor and is very commonly mistaken for a shower.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.220
This is not a shower

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.380
I repeat.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.580
THIS IS NOT A SHOWER.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.140
It is, however, used to freshen yourself up when taking care of your personal hygiene.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.940
A secret technique known only to the chosen few

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.060
who attend on their arduous journey of internally gagging every fifth person they pass.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.580
Be especially careful of any tightly packed gaming room

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.120
as such spaces can be prone to their own independent climate with increased humidity,

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.880
comparable to tropical rain forests.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.500
Now that you're all ready to enjoy the convention,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.020
let's see what's going on.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.260
The most obvious is the dealer's room which scientifically functions as a black hole for your wallet.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.349
This is usually the busiest place at the convention so add a big

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:50.320
con you can expect the walking speed to average out at about one millimeter per hour

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.780
if you do ever find yourself in this kind of situation,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:57.119
it's the perfect time to just stand around in a large group doing nothing, as it's sure to inconvenient and annoy

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.560
absolutely no one ever.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.940
You may notice when in the hall, the environment conditions you to bypass your logical brain in order to make as

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.100
many irrational purchases as possible.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.800
This phenomenon is known as Con Buyers High

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.940
and once infected, it can only be stopped when the individual looks at their wallets and eventually

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.670
realizes that they aren't going to be able to pay the next three months of rent.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.900
Panels are also a massive part of conventions.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.600
There will be many different panels running.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.760
But if there is a popular panel you want to attend, make sure you set up camp at least seven months before the panel starts.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.680
But be wary that the line will still probably be over capacity just before your turn.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.560
They can range from many different topics and shows and a lot of them allow you to ask questions,

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.200
if you ever wanted more insight.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:37.620
Once the panel was nearing its end, it's not any time for the quickfire questions to get through as many people as they can.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.759
Unfortunately, even if you have a burning insightful question nobody has asked yet,

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.980
this is the time which guarantees the next person will take up 15 minutes asking the panelists,

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.680
what brand of shampoo they use that morning?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.520
Other important areas you can check out is,

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.940
the artists' alley where you'll buy quality trinkets you'll lose in a day,

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.640
the gaming room, where you'll get your ass kicked by at least 10 different people more practiced than you,

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.240
and the main lobby where you can hang out and crowd watch

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.800
and definitely not judge the 50 people walking past you who shouts our dead memes.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.460
As you'll be having so much fun and wanting to spend as much time at the con as possible,

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.640
normal living habits may become somewhat of a nuisance

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.020
that takes time away from things you want to do.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.580
Case in point, food.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.200
Food will turn from part of your daily routine to something you'll have to consciously consider.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.020
Where you'll be surviving the weekend on a standard dietary recommendation of

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.560
pizza, burger, instant ramen, and chips.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.580
Now though, this is the recommended diet.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:27.449
You'll find that often times you have to make an important choice between going to that one events you plan to and eating.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.479
One is a panel of sweaty nerds talking about cartoons,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.560
and the other is your normal daily routine that every human needs in order to get energy

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.160
and survive.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.760
So now that you've gone two days without eating a meal

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.360
you may feel your body shutting down and you need to find a place to eat.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.780
This could be the right time to venture further outside the convention to find the proper restaurants.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:47.940
Be warned, however.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:52.020
As the further away you venture from the venue, the closer you are to normal society again.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.680
Which can be deadly for any con-goer.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:59.880
Luckily, this is something you can calculate as if you open up google maps and mark off the area around the convention,

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.820
the Weeb density is inversely proportionate

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.400
to the distance traveled away from the convention in miles.

00:06:04.409 --> 00:06:06.500
This is known as the Weeb-Boltzmann Law,

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.440
and this area marked off right here is the safe zone.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.759
Unless, of course, your city has an area with a high concentration

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.660
of Japanese or Korean restaurants.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.900
In which case, they become temporary embassies for weebs in times of trouble.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:20.480
As you'll likely be going in a group, it's improbable that you'll be able to convince everyone

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.220
to go for a healthy meal option.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:26.060
So, if you want to eat healthy during the convention then my best advice to you is -

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.540
you're fucked.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.520
On some rare occasions, the convention may be held at the hotel or venue

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:33.960
when normal people are staying.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.600
Which can end up becoming one of those unintentionally amusing things

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:40.340
watching them trying to figure out exactly what new planet they've just woken up on.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:44.160
If this happens, don't be afraid to show them that we are JUST normal people.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:44.920
Say hi.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.840
Ask them what they do for a living, what they're here for,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.420
and which one of the monogatari girls they'd prefer to have sit on them.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.660
If you want a packet in early, note that, there are probably

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.100
activities still going on after hours.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.940
Many conventions hold raves.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.340
A place where you either get to see

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.860
a large group of awkward anime fans bouncing around and clapping,

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:03.940
or people who are confident enough to try dancing by attempting to waterbend.

00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:05.780
This is not to be confused with idol shows,

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.490
which is the only place in universe

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:11.600
you'll be able to see a concert hall full of anime nerds go absolutely fucking mental.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.680
For many others, however,

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:16.240
after-hours activities will just boil down to finding a place to consume enough alcohol

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.780
to poison a fucking elephant.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.960
Once you've gone through all that, congratulations.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:26.560
You have survived and hopefully enjoyed your anime convention now comes the hardest part, the post-con.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.020
You know that story you always hear about people waking up from their hangovers

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.060
after a hard night of drinking and feeling like death when they see the sunlight?

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.400
Well, It's a bit like that.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.060
Except the hangover is your post-con blues and the sunlight

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.139
is the crippling depression you feel when you realize

00:07:39.139 --> 00:07:40.530
that you're back in normal society.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:42.640
You can't shout out memes casually.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.820
Everyone's wearing boring normal clothes and nobody wants your free hugs anymore.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.520
Actually, maybe no one ever wanted your free hugs.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.340
Stop trying to give me free hugs.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.900
I don't want free hugs.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.640
GET OUT OF MY PERSONAL SPA -

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.760
That's the typical con experience after a long weekend of anime

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.820
you may find it takes some time to rehabilitate yourself back into society.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.620
But once you do, you will realize that despite all the possible

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:07.880
shortcomings you had an absolutely fantastic time and you want to go to as many

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.140
conventions as possible only to forget that your wallet

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.880
had already put out a hit on you as you don't have any money to pay

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.280
next month's rent because of that figurine you bought.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.340
You stupid anime trash fu-

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:20.620
♪~

